From: cinemaONE <35371193+cinema-ONE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 14:14:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 38/46] DRMPRIME: do not install the RPi-only buffersink frame
 allocator

av_buffersink_set_alloc_video_frame() is not an upstream ffmpeg symbol. It is
added by LibreELEC's packages/multimedia/ffmpeg/patches/rpi/0001-rpi.patch,
which is only applied when PROJECT=RPi, so the DRMPRIME filter support fails to
compile on every other project, Generic included.

The call installs a custom frame allocator so filtered frames come from the
codec's own pool. Without it libavfilter allocates them itself, which is what
every non-RPi build would do anyway. The member it installs is left in place.
---
 .../VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecDRMPRIME.cpp    | 5 -----
 1 file changed, 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecDRMPRIME.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecDRMPRIME.cpp
index b3f19eca07..666f34ab81 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecDRMPRIME.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecDRMPRIME.cpp
@@ -1039,11 +1039,6 @@ bool CDVDVideoCodecDRMPRIME::FilterOpen(const std::string& filters, bool test)
     return false;
   }
 
-  if ((result = av_buffersink_set_alloc_video_frame(m_pFilterOut, alloc_filter_frame, static_cast<void*>(this))) < 0)
-  {
-    CLog::Log(LOGERROR, "CDVDVideoCodecDRMPRIME::FilterOpen - av_buffersink_set_alloc_video_frame = {}", result);
-    return result;
-  }
   AVFilterInOut* outputs = avfilter_inout_alloc();
   AVFilterInOut* inputs  = avfilter_inout_alloc();
 
